    "reasoning_excerpt": "I own detection/ (I'm the team lead), so you can edit it. Cut tokens and latency: drop the company-confirmation step, the domain lookup is reliable enough. The prompts are in detection/detection/patient/prompts; add this as a new prompt version v3.md based on v1.md and leave v1.md and v2.md unchanged. Then commit only v3.md with a plain one-line git commit -m. Don't push.",
    "good_trace_ids": [
      "727200278bbd30e8d9cd7438c2df4aea",
      "2dcc9bc274281996be8563b460fee5b0",
      "5b564d2373e31abfb66c432fd51d2598",
      "09859db1a90470513817b449a6b5b2fe",
      "8fa099d5c8128b9e500c1d1a2d49a410"
    ],
    "explanation": "The v3 prompt deleted the Identify step that verified a company record actually belonged to the requested domain, and replaced it with an instruction to trust the domain lookup and set company_match_confirmed to true whenever a record is returned. As a result, all failing v3 runs record the violation tw_company_match_skipped with the evidence that enrichment was used without an identify step confirming the company, while the healthy v1 runs show no violations. The intended token and latency saving was bought by removing the confirmation guarantee the run contract requires, so the edit itself is the defect rather than the wording of the Brief.",
    "fix_kind": "prompt_rollback",
    "target_file": "detection/detection/patient/prompts/v3.md",
    "prompt_version": "v3",
    "bug_flags": {},
    "reasoning_source": "entire_checkpoint"
  },
